\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Ummm, interesting at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really like where that red dot ended up hehe. If you don't mind me asking, where do you currently reside (which country/continent)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T06:21:14-08:00","id":310155,"title":"","content":"Europe=&gt;Spain=&gt;Galicia if we go from wide to specific.<br /> <br /> Galicia is a somewhat rural/coastal Autonomous Comunity (a literal translation of Comunidad Aut\u00f3noma, the big pieces that Spain is composed off, as States in the USA. Well, sort of) that has its own language, the Galician, that shares roots with Portuguese on top of the Spanish that is common around the country.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I found my positioning interesting because I actually expected it to be more towards Authoritarian though still under the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  messed up sentence flow 11-12-2014, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T06:22:00-08:00","id":310160,"title":"","content":"I generally describe myself as a small-government socialist because there are some things that are too important to be trusted to private enterprise, but Government tends to implement one-size-fits-all solutions for everything else.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-6.75&amp;soc=-7.54\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T07:15:14-08:00","id":310220,"title":"","content":"Hmm...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-8.12&amp;soc=-3.54\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Compared to last presidential candidates <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/charts/crowdgraphpng.php?Mitt_Romney=7.0%2C6.5&amp;Barack_Obama=6.0%2C6.0&amp;Virgil_Goode=9.0%2C9.0&amp;Gary_Johnson=9.5%2C0.0&amp;Rocky_Anderson=4.5%2C-2.0&amp;Jill_Stein=-3.0%2C-3.0&amp;Stewart_Alexander=-5.0%2C-2.0&amp;You=-8.1%2C-3.5&lt;div style=\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Heh...Romney and Obama...no wonder I didn't like either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T09:34:19-08:00","id":310336,"title":"","content":"So I'm in the green square, too:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-4.88&amp;soc=-3.64\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T09:51:10-08:00","id":310345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310160#post310160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally describe myself as a small-government socialist because there are some things that are too important to be trusted to private enterprise, but Government tends to implement one-size-fits-all solutions for everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-5.38&amp;soc=-5.03\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I too am a small government socialist but clearly our differences in graph plotting means we must fight to the death! <br /> <br /> Someone fetch the knives of amiable reconciliation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T12:01:31-08:00","id":310420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310345#post310345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too am a small government socialist but clearly our differences in graph plotting means we must fight to the death!<br /> <br /> Someone fetch the knives of amiable reconciliation!</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as we all side with the purrletariat, there's no need for that.<br /> <img src=\"http://www.quickmeme.com/img/5f/5fd5dadc6606e51bf509ec4ef833eb9d8a46e3dd923c0b527b12e1be638e1630.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T12:06:42-08:00","id":310421,"title":"","content":"I think it is positive that we have small-government socialists on this thread. I tend to view large and powerful structures (be they governments or corporations) as susceptible to corruption and abuse. How would you imagine your strand of socialism to come to fruition and what would that resemble?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T12:10:20-08:00","id":310425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310155#post310155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Europe=&gt;Spain=&gt;Galicia if we go from wide to specific.<br /> <br /> Galicia is a somewhat rural/coastal Autonomous Comunity (a literal translation of Comunidad Aut\u00f3noma, the big pieces that Spain is composed off, as States in the USA. Well, sort of) that has its own language, the Galician, that shares roots with Portuguese on top of the Spanish that is common around the country.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I found my positioning interesting because I actually expected it to be more towards Authoritarian though still under the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting, given Spain's economy since the Great Recession of the 21st century. How are things over there? We basically experienced a drop from developed to developing economy. Latest bit of news I heard was that children faint at school from hunger and some resort to stealing foodstuff from their wealthier classmates. Youth unemployment (under 30s) is nearly at 70%.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T12:21:40-08:00","id":310442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310421#post310421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is positive that we have small-government socialists on this thread. I tend to view large and powerful structures (be they governments or corporations) as susceptible to corruption and abuse. How would you imagine your strand of socialism to come to fruition and what would that resemble?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the things I'd want to see are already being discussed. Universal Healthcare (I like Canada's version), Minimum Income, open borders, expansion of public transportation, decriminalization of drugs. It's the larger cultural changes like destroying the myth of the thin blue line, putting science, technology, and education at the forefront of our policy, combating the surveillance state, those will be even tougher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T13:21:05-08:00","id":310502,"title":"","content":"I'm a big advocate for a fiat currency where we use bees.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly certain I fall into that green block somewhere too, though I have to say I cringe pretty hard at being labeled as a Libertarian.<br /> <br /> Since a lot of you guys seem to have a particular bent to your politics, how do you feel about that label? Does it feel misapplied, appropriate or just irrelevant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T13:53:22-08:00","id":310523,"title":"","content":"I'm solidly in the green quadrant. Knew that already. Despite some strong disagreements which specific policies that are associated with it.<br /> <br /> To Leetsepeak question about the libertarian label:<br /> <br /> I think the problem is that the radical right in the USA has misappropriated the term. The majority of the &quot;libertarian&quot; identifying politicians are not actually libertarians once they're in power. It gets conflated with lots of policy platforms that are not inherently based on libertarian philosophy.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with being considered libertarian in the context of the chart presented, because it is closer to the general philosophy that puts individual liberty over government authority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:07:08-08:00","id":310556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310425#post310425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting, given Spain's economy since the Great Recession of the 21st century. How are things over there? We basically experienced a drop from developed to developing economy. Latest bit of news I heard was that children faint at school from hunger and some resort to stealing foodstuff from their wealthier classmates. Youth unemployment (under 30s) is nearly at 70%.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are those data from Spain or your country? Which one is it,by the way?<br /> <br /> We... are doing fine all things considered. Well, Spain as country is, only european country to grow as of late economically speaking. People though, not so fine. Unemployment is still a very big problem, but then again, it always was around here. Too dependant on tourism.<br /> <br /> We have some social movements that aglutinated in new political parties that seem to be getting wide support from the people (Podemos). We also have some independentist movements, specially in Catalu\u00f1a (Catalonia) they even made sort of a referendum but not really to ask the people if they wanted to seceed from Spain and be their own country. The people in charge seem to think it was a sound success, I wouldn't call that to way less than a third of the population voting Yes, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:41:09-08:00","id":310571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310502#post310502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big advocate for a fiat currency where we use bees.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly certain I fall into that green block somewhere too, though I have to say I cringe pretty hard at being labeled as a Libertarian.<br /> <br /> Since a lot of you guys seem to have a particular bent to your politics, how do you feel about that label? Does it feel misapplied, appropriate or just irrelevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat inaccurate, but that's the nature of simple survey systems. A lot of my politics are all over the place depending on what you ask. For example on gun control I have views that cause people to scream and call me a facist that wants to take away their guns, at the same time others scream that I support school shootings. It's amusing in it's own way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:53:11-08:00","id":310576,"title":"","content":"I feel your pain there Odd_Canuck.<br /> <br /> Between the trend in politics to push away from center, and lots of policies focusing on symptoms instead of causes, advocating for practical centrist solutions often feels odd.<br /> <br /> I was actually recently having a discussion with someone else about the illusionary nature of security, and what makes people <i>feel</i> safer is often very far from what actually makes them safer; and the difficulty of trying to explain the difference. I brought up a school I spent some time working in. It had metal detectors, five armed police officers, and a freaking holding cell in it because of the violence that's happened there. And despite all that one of the teachers got attacked with a machete by a student. Anyone that thinks there's a simple solution to that... boggles my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T16:26:48-08:00","id":310667,"title":"","content":"I only regularly read one left wing newspaper because right wing ones here are too gonzo for me. I'm right winger, but I prefer reading a newspaper run by one old Communist politician who is independent enough to mock everything, including himself.<br /> <br /> Right Wing newspapers here are either embracing neoliberalism zealously (OK, I'm liberal, but ideal of completely free market is in friction with reality, and compromises are needed), writing conspiracy theories about Russians being responsible for everything (Jews are out of fashion) or writing conspiracy theories about Demons and Vampires that would make Long Night of Vigil blush.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-12-2014, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T16:43:44-08:00","id":310702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310667#post310667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only regularly read one left wing newspaper because right wing ones here are too gonzo for me. I'm right winger, but I prefer reading a newspaper run by one old Communist politician who is independent enough to mock everything, including himself.<br /> <br /> Right Wing newspapers here are either embracing neoliberalism zealously (OK, I'm liberal, but ideal of completely free market is in friction with reality, and compromises are needed), writing conspiracy theories about Russians being responsible for everything (Jews are out of fashion) or writing conspiracy theories about Demons and Vampires that would make Long Night of Vigil blush.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's less Right Wing, and more Crazy Person","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T16:46:22-08:00","id":310706,"title":"","content":"How Left and Right ideals are defined in the US are very different in other countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T16:58:48-08:00","id":310726,"title":"","content":"Polish Left Wing is probably Right Wing in many countries. I think of myself as a right winger in more general sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:31:37-08:00","id":310989,"title":"","content":"Ugh, no middle options on that quiz. It's all two variations of two directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:42:38-08:00","id":310994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310989#post310989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, no middle options on that quiz. It's all two variations of two directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember about ten months ago, I was looking for a political scale to use as part of my thesis work (was looking to include a measure of political leaning, an aspect I've since dialed back), and I came across it, thought the same thing.<br /> <br /> That said, I couldn't find a useful political attitudes scale anyway. They tend to be local in nature, plus political attitudes have waay too many dimensions to easily measure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:50:10-08:00","id":311001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310556#post310556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are those data from Spain or your country? Which one is it,by the way?<br /> <br /> We... are doing fine all things considered. Well, Spain as country is, only european country to grow as of late economically speaking. People though, not so fine. Unemployment is still a very big problem, but then again, it always was around here. Too dependant on tourism.<br /> <br /> We have some social movements that aglutinated in new political parties that seem to be getting wide support from the people (Podemos). We also have some independentist movements, specially in Catalu\u00f1a (Catalonia) they even made sort of a referendum but not really to ask the people if they wanted to seceed from Spain and be their own country. The people in charge seem to think it was a sound success, I wouldn't call that to way less than a third of the population voting Yes, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for Greece. Things have gotten so bad that a law was passed forbidding mention of suicides caused by the economy in media. The reasoning behind the punitive (for the middle and lower classes) Greek measures scares me, just like the fact that so many Europeans backed punishment for our case (<a href=\"http://blogs.ft.com/brusselsblog/2014/11/11/draghis-ecb-management-the-leaked-geithner-files/\" target=\"_blank\">Geithner apparently leaked to the FT</a> that European officials wanted to contain the crisis in Greece only and then proceed to &quot;crush&quot; us). I was always against punishing an entire people for the crimes of its leader (an eye for an eye leaves the whole world blind), let alone send a nation to social hell and a polarised, violent political life just for overspending and internal corruption.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:57:08-08:00","id":311009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=310576#post310576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel your pain there Odd_Canuck.<br /> <br /> Between the trend in politics to push away from center, and lots of policies focusing on symptoms instead of causes, advocating for practical centrist solutions often feels odd.<br /> <br /> I was actually recently having a discussion with someone else about the illusionary nature of security, and what makes people <i>feel</i> safer is often very far from what actually makes them safer; and the difficulty of trying to explain the difference. I brought up a school I spent some time working in. It had metal detectors, five armed police officers, and a freaking holding cell in it because of the violence that's happened there. And despite all that one of the teachers got attacked with a machete by a student. Anyone that thinks there's a simple solution to that... boggles my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do politics <b>actually</b> move away from the center, or just political rhetoric? I have a deep respect for classical liberals, civic republicans advocating deliberative democracy and the likes, and I think part of the reason the USSR failed was its deep disregard for (direct) democratic procedures, which it labelled as &quot;bourgeoisie pseudo-democracy&quot;, whereas Marx (a lover of the Classical) envisioned the socialist/communist state as one of direct, participative democracy that would come about and flourish only in those countries whose citizens have achieved an advanced democracy and economy (and nothing like Tsarist Russia).<br /> <br /> Perhaps politics moves, in theory or practice, away from the center exactly because the balance of power has been messed up? We have enough quantitative data to be able to claim that wealth and power are being accumulated (by the &quot;dreadful 1%&quot;). It might not lead to the dystopia some predict, but it can't be good regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:07:55-08:00","id":311013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=311009#post311009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But do politics <b>actually</b> move away from the center, or just political rhetoric?</div> </div> </div> </div>I said &quot;trend&quot; for a reason. Not as a constant, inevitable, or irreversible thing. And yes, there's ample evidence that this is not just rhetoric. The push in many countries towards austerity is an actual policy decision that was fueled by polarized politics, not centrist economic considerations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps politics moves, in theory or practice, away from the center exactly because the balance of power has been messed up? </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, yes. Populations, as whole, and practically tautologically, are centrist/populist. The majority of the population are not ideologues. Thus the evenly distributed the power is in a democracy, the more easy it is for it to skew off of center.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T02:29:12-08:00","id":311038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=311001#post311001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's for Greece. Things have gotten so bad that a law was passed forbidding mention of suicides caused by the economy in media. The reasoning behind the punitive (for the middle and lower classes) Greek measures scares me, just like the fact that so many Europeans backed punishment for our case (<a href=\"http://blogs.ft.com/brusselsblog/2014/11/11/draghis-ecb-management-the-leaked-geithner-files/\" target=\"_blank\">Geithner apparently leaked to the FT</a> that European officials wanted to contain the crisis in Greece only and then proceed to &quot;crush&quot; us). I was always against punishing an entire people for the crimes of its leader (an eye for an eye leaves the whole world blind), let alone send a nation to social hell and a polarised, violent political life just for overspending and internal corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Greece. Sorry to hear that things are actually as bad as they seemed. I don't think they are fooling anyone banning that sort of information, I'm not that naive to beliebe those things stoped hapening all of a sudden from one day to the next when they were a thing.<br /> It's always the same, isn't it? Some people in power mess it up big time but is the people who has to deal with the consecuences. Here we (because I don't know where people think the money the goberment manages comes from) payed to save a bunch of banks that then refused to invest that money in the country, they basically made the whole thing went banckrupt and yet they gave themselves millions in indemnizations, all of this while kicking whole families out of their houses if they so dared to be late on the last month of their morgage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T13:07:34-08:00","id":311580,"title":"","content":"I've taken those tests before and I usually land somewhere in the green. More towards the Left and less towards Libertarian. Which is no surprise as I place people, life, liberty and the living world before businesses, governments, stupidity and greed.<br /> <br /> Walking away before the flames singe my ass hairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T17:32:09-08:00","id":311792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"b