c=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T03:48:31-08:00","id":312858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=312158#post312158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess being pro-LBGT puts me in more leftist spectrum for some, but on another hand I have allergy towards tumblr's SJWs, who to be frank generally don't do anything meaningful rather than ranting.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gf is bi and when we met I was religious and conservative (and also 17 and naive). We've been together for more than 6 years and I've watched friends walk out on us as a couple because of this, so I consider myself pro-LGBT. However, we wouldn't join an LGBT organisation that doesn't stand for wider economic and social justice, just like we wouldn't a vegetarian or environmentalist group, even though we are both. We believe in class consciousness in the Marxist sense.<br /> <br /> Plus, making a big deal out of sexual identity is playing the game of homophobes on their own terms. My gf, for example, does not want others to view her as who she would sleep with.<br /> <br /> Would a tolerant but corporate-run society be <i>really</i> an improvement? Slightly, yes. But if I'm going to raise a banner and take to the streets, I'd do it for socialism and direct democracy. On the other hand, lobbying for the inclusion of progressive LGBT demands in the agenda of the Left, is something I not only agree with but actively do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 11-15-2014, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T03:57:59-08:00","id":312860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=311580#post311580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've taken those tests before and I usually land somewhere in the green. More towards the Left and less towards Libertarian. Which is no surprise as I place people, life, liberty and the living world before businesses, governments, stupidity and greed.<br /> <br /> Walking away before the flames singe my ass hairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be surprised by how many people I have met, including people from Greece, who are pro-greed and pro-corporate...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> His opinion isn't even the most arguable on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I know. But I mean well, doesn't that count for something? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Plus, I rarely argue politics and when I do, I try to avoid the logical fallacies of philosophical debate. So, in most cases, discussions with people I disagree with prove fruitful for both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 11-15-2014, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T07:01:56-08:00","id":312922,"title":"","content":"There are two very general issues in US politics; Financial; and Social. The financial issue (primarily taxes) is far larger in scope and is pretty much locked in by conservative thought. Whenever someone brings such up as in taxes, the social issues suddenly become in play and &quot;abortion&quot; and Gay Rights&quot; become the topics bandied about, and all the while any financial issue does a fade. It's one of the reasons why Obama never came out in support of gay marriage (until Biden opened his mouth. Despite what rumor says, I refuse to believe that his big mouth was a calculated move. It was a genuine blunder) Obama didn't want to say anything outright because it' takes away political chips on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T13:13:41-08:00","id":313219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if I'm going to raise a banner and take to the streets, I'd do it for socialism and direct democracy. </div> </div> </div>Direct democracy is just a pipe dream, since representative democracy is more efficient model to run nation states. Not even cities can be run that way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:48:56-08:00","id":313309,"title":"","content":"Pipe dream or not it's something to aspire to. In my country at least most of the people are very disatisfied with representative democracy. There are also things were direct democracy seems like the only decent alternative to take a decision, ineficcient and non-viable as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T15:08:06-08:00","id":313320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=313219#post313219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Direct democracy is just a pipe dream, since representative democracy is more efficient model to run nation states. Not even cities can be run that way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A brilliant lecturer I had at uni, albeit one with whom I disagreed quite often, said that we should plan and design our polities based on the ideal citizen we would like to see emerge from participating, not the current citizenry.<br /> <br /> Direct democracy was pretty effective in ancient Athens and in other cases (including the ill-fated Paris Commune). It was when they had to face enormous, anti-democratic forces that some failed (while others stood their ground). Some representation will be in place, but the citizenry will have the final say on what laws are ratified and which politicians are, at any time, recalled. My experience as a Greek citizen has also made me very suspicious of political parties as institutions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=313309#post313309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pipe dream or not it's something to aspire to. In my country at least most of the people are very disatisfied with representative democracy. There are also things were direct democracy seems like the only decent alternative to take a decision, ineficcient and non-viable as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every alternative is a pipe dream until it comes to fruition. Imagine explaining our system to serfs of the feudal era, or the medieval religious monarchies to ancient Athenians!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 11-15-2014, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T15:15:34-08:00","id":313323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A brilliant lecturer I had at uni, albeit one with whom I disagreed quite often, said that we should plan and design our polities based on the ideal citizen we would like to see emerge from participating, not the current citizenry. </div> </div> </div>Ideal. Yeeep, There is no such thing in this world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Direct democracy was pretty effective in ancient Athens and in other cases (including the ill-fated Paris Commune). It was when they had to face enormous, anti-democratic forces that some failed (while others stood their ground). Some representation will be in place, but the citizenry will have the final say on what laws are ratified and which politicians are, at any time, recalled. My experience as a Greek citizen has also made me very suspicious of political parties as institutions. </div> </div> </div>Funny thing you mention Athens, since it exactly only worked in long term because select few actually could participate for direct democracy to be feasible there.<br /> <br /> And I don't trust citizenry also, as I cannot trust amateurs to ratify any single law, and politicians will fear to make unpopular but necessary decisions. There are rarely decisions made that necessitate popular vote.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T18:25:10-08:00","id":314083,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm a leftist, though I don't agree w ith the majority of &quot;leftist&quot; positions(identity politics, progressive history, economic arrangements, etc.). My PC results are economic -9.7, social -10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T04:31:32-08:00","id":314370,"title":"","content":"I should really create Right Wing thread, balance demands it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T04:51:34-08:00","id":314383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-7.00&amp;soc=-5.33\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-7.00&amp;soc=-5.33\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-7.00&amp;soc=-5.33\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=-7.00&amp;soc=-5.33 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T05:09:08-08:00","id":314391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/printablegraph?ec=2.38&amp;soc=-0.97\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/images/minicomALL.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/printablegraph?ec=2.38&amp;soc=-0.97\" target=\"_blank\"> The Political Compass </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/printablegraph?ec=2.38&amp;soc=-0.97\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.politicalcompass.org/printablegraph?ec=2.38&amp;soc=-0.97 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yep, a right winger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T01:27:00-08:00","id":315174,"title":"","content":"I will ignite the fires around here, but still it is my opinion and I don't want to force them upon anyone. <br /> <br /> Bottom line, people are stupid. The masses are ignorant by default AND by choice. In the USA people watch Honey Boo Boo, in the EU people watch Secret Story. The most read newspapers are Sports and Gossip/Tabloids. The Kardashians are the idols of a generation. THIS represents the MAJORITY and who decides in a Democracy? The majority! Direct Democracy would never work, the people are not fit to decide anything. It's clich\u00e9 but I hold as an absolute truth, Democracy is the worst form of Government except for all others that have been tried. I defend it because the alternatives have always been atrocious, but it is still bad.<br /> <br /> Despite my ideals leaning towards libertarianism I still support an authoritative Government (up to a degree, nothing is more precious than freedom and I will oppose any ideology that restricts it). People need to be told what to do, they are not fit to decide. As much as it pains all of us, the most successful governments were dictatorships. They led to the greatest development of their countries. Why? Because they could do what they wanted how they wanted without red tape nor the approval of the masses. Now you will say the price is too high or even unthinkable and I will agree with you. That's why I will keep supporting Democracy, using my single vote to try to change my country to better and pretend the direct democracy mechanisms I have in my Constitution (which are actually many and powerful if only in theory) actually work and mean something.<br /> <br /> It's frustrating living in a country of unlimited potential, one of the few who could close it's borders and live by its natural resources without needing anything from anyone and still be one of the most underdeveloped, indebted and backwards countries in EU. I thank all my corrupt governments of these last 40 years of Democracy that dishonoured those who fought to end the dictatorship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T02:10:43-08:00","id":315201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=315174#post315174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bottom line, people are stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the issue. There's plenty of evidence that this old adage isn't actually true. The whole crowd-sourcing boom is because if you get enough people together in the right context, they'll often pick/produce the best/optimal answer.<br /> <br /> You can't really judge people on popular media. There's been cheap low brow entertainment for the masses for as long as there's been masses. It's not a reflection of our decision making abilities. It's a reflection of how, ultimately, our brains like simple and comfortable things when we want to relax. Poop jokes are a cheap laugh, and we want to have cheap laughs because we don't want to blow our mental budgets just to chuckle for a few seconds.<br /> <br /> Entertainment doesn't actually represent the majority. Especially since entertainment is not created by the masses. Game of Thrones is also popular as hell, but it's on HBO for a reason. It's too damned expensive for broadcast TV. &quot;Reality&quot; TV dominates the airwaves because it's so cheap to make, that it is impossibly more profitable for most channels than other content. Then you're left with what kind of cheap-to-make TV you're going to watch because that's what all the channels are flooding you with.<br /> <br /> Even if you're trying to consume media that isn't low brow, like watching educational TV, oh wait remember what channel Honey Boo Boo is on... Or watching the news? Yeah, our journalists are actually pretty bad at informing us if you look at the attempts to study how well informed and knowledge regular views of cable news are.<br /> <br /> The problem can't actually be definitely put on the masses. The masses need systems that work for them. That's the whole point of having that government thing. The government needs to create systems where the masses can be in the right context to make the decisions they're actually pretty good at doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As much as it pains all of us, the most successful governments were dictatorships. </div> </div> </div>Define success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T02:54:23-08:00","id":315208,"title":"","content":"Actually entertainment IS created by the masses. The channels broadcast what the masses want in savage struggle for Audience Ratings. They put out what people want to see. I.E. The History Channel: perhaps the best channel I've ever seen since I got cable for the first time. What is the History Channel nowadays? Reality TV. I can't remember the last time I actually watched a documentary on the History Channel. And this is a SPECIFIC channel, supposedly targeting an educated audience with an interest in History. But the pressure of audiences made them appeal to the mainstream low thinking audiences. If you go to the mainstream channels it gets much much worse.<br /> <br /> Game of Thrones is popular? Compare the ratings with Reality TV, more compare the ratings to other cable series that are much worse but deliver the easy clich\u00e9s. GoT is popular for it's genre, but could never compete in a ratings war. Movies are the same. The theatres are filled with plastic remakes that become blockbusters and even win Oscars delivering mind-numbing shit.<br /> <br /> Everyone worried about Orwell's distopia but are gladly walking into Huxley's one!<br /> <br /> And yes, it affects people's decision making. Because of easy entertainment and cheap laughs, the decisions will also me easy, cheap and worst of all uninformed. And I might add, a lot of countries but mine in particular (it's the one I know better lol) people vote for party almost like a club. They like Team X win or lose and do the same for Party X &quot;I've always voted for X, even my father was for Party X, I'll vote X&quot;.<br /> <br /> When people can't even point their city on the map, you expect them to ponder which candidate will do the best or even learn about their Government Program? I doubt most people even knows the party they are voting for program much less the alternatives.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;</i><i>There's been cheap low brow entertainment for the masses for as long as there's been masses&quot; </i><br /> <br /> That's why the masses never decided squat and the minorities always did as they pleased. The 1% rules the world and the other 99% smile and clap hands.<br /> <br /> You focused an interesting point: <b>Journalists</b>. They are worst than ever. Hardly any investigation, online controversial headlines, one sided half-truths, it's scary! And I got further, one of the things that pains the most is assassination of my native language. People speak bad and write worse. There was a time you'd look up to a Lawyer and a Journalist as an example of perfect and amazing use of language, nowadays I watch the news and see a COMMUNICATION PROFESSIONAL speaking almost like the uneducated average Joe. That contributes to lowering the brow of the masses.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;</i><i>The problem can't actually be definitely put on the masses. The masses need systems that work for them. That's the whole point of having that government thing. The government needs to create systems where the masses can be in the right context to make the decisions they're actually pretty good at doing.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I disagree with the fact they are good at doing, but the rest I sign it with you. That should be the aim (or at least one of them) of any government left or right.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Define success.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Job creation, education, economy, healthcare, general improvement of population's quality of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T02:57:30-08:00","id":315211,"title":"","content":"I took the test but..uh it's kind of simplistic. I knew I would be strongly on the Left side. But the questions are rather simplistic and I don't identify with American style libertarianism at all. Interesting, but flawed little site there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T08:43:10-08:00","id":315427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=315208#post315208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;</i><i>The problem can't actually be definitely put on the masses. The masses need systems that work for them. That's the whole point of having that government thing. The government needs to create systems where the masses can be in the right context to make the decisions they're actually pretty good at doing.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I disagree with the fact they are good at doing, but the rest I sign it with you. That should be the aim (or at least one of them) of any government left or right.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually the bit that, in part, drove me to reach the policies I personally have... that and having to write software that had to deal with allowing flags to avoid overtime and the like for a situation that involved multiple different union contracts, which of course would change every few years. Hence why I strongly favor automation and independent systems, particularly as we move into an information age. Let a computer draw the election boundaries. Draw up a contract once, with allowances for variation over time, rather than renegotiating every point every 4 years. Don't have a fixed minimum wage, tie it to a managed basket of cost of living expenses and do adjustments automatically every year. Better still, go with the even more simple solution of every legal resident getting a fixed living expense from the government that covers all basic needs (and tie the amount into a basket of CoL expenses), and with one higher-tax stroke you eliminate the need for welfare, minimum wage and all the welfare-to-work headaches that go along with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:10:44-08:00","id":315529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=315208#post315208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually entertainment IS created by the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It really isn't. The large number of both critically acclaimed and fan loved shows that get cancelled for complete shit is proof enough that the entertainment industry does not give a shit about what the masses want. The masses, by in large, are the product being sold in entertainment, not the customers. Your analysis of this isn't really based on how the economics of this work.<br /> <br /> As the newer adage goes, if it's free, you're the product. And that's the thing. TV doesn't exist for us to pay for entertainment we want. TV exists for production companies to sell ad space. Even with Cable/Dish you're only paying for access, not for content. The content's customers are the companies seeking ad space, not the masses.<br /> <br /> Popular entertainment has nothing to do with how smart people act as a group. Because it isn't a valid metric of what people decide as a group. The masses aren't actually making any decisions.<br /> <br /> What people want to see is only a fraction of the equation of what gets put on air. And here's where being a lefty shines. Where does the best TV come from? The Masses. While publicly funded TV has had its problems, but it generally maintains much higher quality programming. When the viewers are actually the customers - and not the product - the quality gets better. Reading Rainbow continues to move on because the masses actually got engaged in ensuring it get created rather than letting the TV industry grind out a good educational show.<br /> <br /> This even is observable in journalism. The more a journalism outlet is funded by their audience rather than their sponsors, the quality of their reporting increases.<br /> <br /> The masses are part of the problem, because democracy, but ultimately everything indicates that more actual democracy rather than more power in the hands of the few makes things better in this regard. Not worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I might add, a lot of countries but mine in particular (it's the one I know better lol) people vote for party almost like a club. They like Team X win or lose and do the same for Party X &quot;I've always voted for X, even my father was for Party X, I'll vote X&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Which is a case for more direct democracy. Parties are a step away from pure democracy. They reduce the power of the masses by, as you've put it, turning voting into an identity issue rather than who's the best candidate/what are the best policies issue.<br /> <br /> The recent USA midterm elections have a great example of this. There were elections where the anti-minimum wage candidate won, but minimum wage increases were passed by referendum. The masses wanted policy X, but voted for the party that's against policy X. Because they get caught up in party identity politics over policy debates, but when the policies were put up for debate without parties, they voted for the economically superior policy option.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of parties for more direct democracy gets around this. It doesn't make it worse.<br /> <br /> Your argument doesn't work, because you're basically saying that democracy doesn't work with examples that are all problematic because power was removed from the masses; not granted to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Job creation, education, economy, healthcare, general improvement of population's quality of life. </div> </div> </div>Democracies win, hands down. Autocracies of any stripe have consistently been exceedingly bad at this for the general population. They're excellent at doing this for the elites, but horrible for doing this for their whole population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T12:09:15-08:00","id":315595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What people want to see is only a fraction of the equation of what gets put on air. And here's where being a lefty shines. Where does the best TV come from? The Masses. While publicly funded TV has had its problems, but it generally maintains much higher quality programming. When the viewers are actually the customers - and not the product - the quality gets better. Reading Rainbow continues to move on because the masses actually got engaged in ensuring it get created rather than letting the TV industry grind out a good educational show. </div> </div> </div>Eh, it probably depends on the country. Our public TV should be privatized because that would be a mercy kill. It either apes commercial stations badly to emulate latest fads or is a propaganda tube for every party that gets their party members into the board. It was good in 1990s, worse in 2000s and a trash now. Especially after Christian right wing cancelled some older good shows for being &quot;Communist&quot; and channeled money from culture oriented channel that was pretty good into religious shows and history shows full of revisionism.<br /> <br /> The conclusion: Better a commercial TV than a public TV that is filled with politicians and their relatives. It is ironical indeed here that one of more independent TV stations is ran by second wealthiest man in Poland. Too much commercials and Home Alone reruns, but their news channel is actually good.<br /> <br /> In the end it depends on who runs given medium. I know one left wing newspaper that became ridiculous in their obsession with pedophile priests, but I read one newspaper ran by an old communist which I read for ironical self-depreciating humor of his, and having balls to mock everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-18-2014, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T13:21:25-08:00","id":315673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=315595#post315595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It either apes commercial stations badly to emulate latest fads or is a propaganda tube for every party that gets their party members into the board. It was good in 1990s, worse in 2000s and a trash now. Especially after Christian right wing cancelled some older good shows for being &quot;Communist&quot; and channeled money from culture oriented channel that was pretty good into religious shows and history shows full of revisionism.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can they do this if the public TV is controlled by the masses instead of by a minority?<br /> <br /> This sounds more like your public TV has been corrupted by a minority getting control of it. Which isn't a flaw in public TV, but a flaw in the systems the government has in place to keep it public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T01:47:17-08:00","id":316064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=315529#post315529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the newer adage goes, if it's free, you're the product. And that's the thing. TV doesn't exist for us to pay for entertainment we want. TV exists for production companies to sell ad space. Even with Cable/Dish you're only paying for access, not for content. The content's customers are the companies seeking ad space, not the masses.<br /> <br /> Popular entertainment has nothing to do with how smart people act as a group. Because it isn't a valid metric of what people decide as a group. The masses aren't actually making any decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If TV exists for production companies sell add space, that's only profitable if they put on shows that blow the audience ratings sky high! Therefore the MASSES DO control entertainment. Critically and popular acclaimed series are cancelled for bullshit reasons because they did not generate enough audience to justify their cost.<br /> <br /> TV puts up the shittiest shows and the audience sky rockets! You gave me Game of Thrones example, but you can add Breaking Bad, House of Cards, Battlestar Gallactica, etc. and none of those will remotely compare with Big Brother, Secret Story, Keeping Up With the Kardashians, etc.<br /> <br /> Because masses are indeed ignorant and want to self destroy the few brain cells they still have. In comparison, the series I mentioned represent a minority in comparison with the bs reality TV I mentioned after.<br /> <br /> I do understand the economy, because if you are selling ad space, that space is worth more the more audiences the TV Program has, that's why nothing is more expensive than Super Bowl half-time! TV Stations need to find programs that bring the greatest numbers in audience ratings to capitalize in their ad space selling.<br /> <br /> Moving on from TV, direct democracy? In my country it works like this, you vote in a party, the most voted party has the most seats in the Parliament and the the President asks the most voted party with the most seats in the Parliament to appoint a Prime-Minister who will form a Government. Parliament has legislative power and controls Government activity who has the executive power and a shared legislative power. The President oversees the acitvities of both.<br /> <br /> Until now it seems quite a normal political system and a representative democracy. But, in addition to all of this, our Constitution foresees that citizens can call up Referendums, submit LAWS for approval, have seats in the galleries of the Parliament to watch over the discussions, submit laws to the Constitutional Court, etc. Do you know how many times that happened in the 40 years of democracy? ZERO! Unless the Commies or the Extreme Left parties were manipulating the events, those were the few times when the &quot;direct democracy&quot; ever happened.<br /> <br /> And finally, in my country anyone can form an official political party as long as you get 5k signatures. Still for the last 40 years only two parties have formed Government and every election we have over 50% abstinence (don't know the best translation, but it means more than half of the registered voters decide not to vote). Why? Because the masses do not care! After the election everyone complaints about those who won, but hardly anyone turned off the TV to go vote, Secret Story voting was more important or some other BS.<br /> <br /> On a final note, mass behaviour is much distinct of individual behaviour, it is so much easier to manipulate the ignorant masses than an educated individual. Especially when people want easy entertainment, easy opinions and mottos to scream. Hardly anyone takes the time to stop and think.<br /> <br /> For one, I do not support my Government. I voted for them, four years ago I believed in their team and thought of them as a fresh start (the youngest candidates ever, a new approach, etc.) but was completely let down and despite doing a lot of good they did so much more bad. Nevertheless, doesn't matter how enraged I am against them, I cannot see myself in the public demonstrations that happened or in most people that complaint about them. Why? Because the masses complaint for complaining. They do not think about what's wrong and how could it be better, they feed on the Opposition (who is greedy for power or at least 15m of attention) bs and repeat it angrily. If you stop one of them and ask questions they soon stop having answers and resort to &quot;Oh you I see you were one of the idiots that voted for them, thanks to you we're in this hole.&quot; or some other form of insult.<br /> <br /> And left shines? Well, like the lady said, socialism works until you spend all of other people's money. (yeah she might have been a cruel b**** but the UK still feeds on the economic turn around she accomplished otherwise they'd be at least as bad as Portugal/Greece if not worse)<br /> <br /> @Odd_Canuck I take you are being sarcastic, but on a note, Denmark does not have a minimum wage (and they voted again against it recently) and still have better wages than most countries in the World (if not all). And with better wages I mean those who are at the bottom have a better income that middle class in my country. Taking out the minimum wage is not necessarily a bad thing.<br /> <br /> And I do not oppose the social state / welfare, but you need a strong economy to support it, otherwise where does the money come from? It's not like we have oil like the US or Norway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T03:12:55-08:00","id":316102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=316064#post316064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If TV exists for production companies sell add space, that's only profitable if they put on shows that blow the audience ratings sky high!</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. Selling the most doesn't mean getting the most profit. If something will cost you ~$20K per episode to produce, and you'll make ~$1M in ad revenue per episode, and another show costs ~$1.5M per episode but it's so awesome you're looking at ~$2M in ad revenue... which wins? The first. It might be half as popular, but it makes way more money. And then everybody is making the cheap profitable less popular shows... until that's almost everything that's on and the audience doesn't actually have a choice besides which schlock they're going to watch.<br /> <br /> You really, really, don't seem to have even a basic grasp of the economic influences that lead to the current US pop culture media and how poorly it represents the masses actual tastes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> TV puts up the shittiest shows and the audience sky rockets! </div> </div> </div>No, they don't. That's the problem. You're assuming that audiences are significantly larger for these shows... when they're not. There's some data sampling issues (a lot of Reality TV shows use live audience participation to drive up audience rankings to avoid people just recording shows and watching them later, which reduces rankings even if the show is popular), but these shows aren't actually statistically super popular. They're just cheap and popular enough that they're more profitable than better and more popular; because better costs too much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You gave me Game of Thrones example, but you can add Breaking Bad, House of Cards, Battlestar Gallactica, etc. and none of those will remotely compare with Big Brother, Secret Story, Keeping Up With the Kardashians, etc. </div> </div> </div>Um...<br /> <br /> GoT is a premium channel program. The rest aren't. Comparisons are apples to oranges (as in there are a significant number of people that cannot afford to watch GoT that can afford Big Brother).<br /> <br /> Breaking Bad's ratings beat the Kardashians with ease, and Big Brother is broadcast not Cable (same problem with GoT).<br /> <br /> House of Cards was a Netflix show making it somewhat irrelevant in comparison (aka it isn't a TV show, it is an Internet show).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moving on from TV, direct democracy? In my country it works like this, you vote in a party, the most voted party has the most seats in the Parliament and the the President asks the most voted party with the most seats in the Parliament to appoint a Prime-Minister who will form a Government. </div> </div> </div>That's not actually a direct democracy. That's a parliamentary representative democracy. As noted earlier, this system doesn't push the masses to decide on policy because it makes voting a matter of political party identity over policy issues. The particulars of your country's parliamentary democracy are also not universal. Lots of parliaments managed to have more than two significant parties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...every election we have over 50% abstinence (don't know the best translation, but it means more than half of the registered voters decide not to vote). Why? Because the masses do not care! </div> </div> </div>Abstention.<br /> <br /> But you're still oversimplifying these things. Vote turn out is a huge issue in lots of countries. Not because the masses are inherently incapable of it (there are countries that have much higher voter turn out), but again this is generally a matter of system failure.<br /> <br /> The USA has countless examples of ways in which the system is structured to discourage voting. In my state a government official blatantly said they passed a law that would discourage voting because the majority supports the other party and suppressing the vote helps avoid the majority coming down on the unpopular party. Which in turns fuels voter apathy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a final note, mass behaviour is much distinct of individual behaviour, it is so much easier to manipulate the ignorant masses than an educated individual. Especially when people want easy entertainment, easy opinions and mottos to scream. Hardly anyone takes the time to stop and think. </div> </div> </div>Educated people are actually very easy to manipulate. Being smart or educated rarely actually stops you from falling for the same psychological tricks used on anyone else. If anything it can make you more susceptible to poor decision making. People that feel they're well informed tend to question their positions less than people that feel they are not well informed; meaning those that don't feel well informed are more likely to actually listen to the facts and consider an individual decision, where those that feel well informed tend to vote with their preconceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And left shines? Well, like the lady said, socialism works until you spend all of other people's money. </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, in the context of that statement... this isn't a problem. If the US taxed political advertising for $0.01 cent for every dollar spent... we could fund PBS indefinitely and a few other nice socialist programs to go with it. We've had single races (so one candidate vs. another, not the whole election cycle, in a single state so not nation wide either) rack up to $100M in ads. There is clearly lots, and lots, of money out there that could be put to better use than politicians yelling bad things at each other on TV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I do not oppose the social state / welfare, but you need a strong economy to support it, otherwise where does the money come from? It's not like we have oil like the US or Norway. </div> </div> </div>You need a strong economy to support any country's activities. A despotic autocrat can't actually make their country rich by declaring it rich. They need resources to turn into economic value just the same as a highly socialist one does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T04:26:41-08:00","id":316136,"title":"","content":"I don't have US exact numbers to make stand on the ratings we're arguing, but for the sake of argument (which is the point) I will do deeper research and see if the numbers support your position or mine on the ratings.<br /> <br /> But regarding being cable/netflix, I watch House of Cards and Game of Thrones both on FOX. They are cable, not internet exclusive.<br /> <br /> Regarding the direct democracy you quoted me on the wrong paragraph, the one you quoted was me giving you an insight how our political system, the next paragraph was the one with the direct democracy mechanisms we have that people do not use.<br /> <br /> Besides what I mentioned above I generally agree with what your wrote in your latest comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:41:30-08:00","id":316363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=316136#post316136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But regarding being cable/netflix, I watch House of Cards and Game of Thrones both on FOX. They are cable, not internet exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different markets, also making this difficult. FOX's main channel in the USA is broadcast. Anyone with a TV and a receiver gets it for free. They can't even show things like Game of Thrones. In the USA ~60% of homes have Cable. So there's a somewhat massive ~40% of Americans that have access to Big Brother, but not Breaking Bad.<br /> <br /> There are more Americans that only have access broadcast TV, than there are HBO subscribers in the world.<br /> <br /> How you watch them is not how they're sold in their primary market. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding the direct democracy you quoted me on the wrong paragraph, the one you quoted was me giving you an insight how our political system, the next paragraph was the one with the direct democracy mechanisms we have that people do not use. </div> </div> </div>The two are fundamentally linked. Representative democracies are prone to having systems that are designed to suppress voting turn out to keep politicians in power by trying to enforce the status quo; which has a chilling effect on direct democracy options available to the masses as they don't have faith in their government (for good reason) but aren't being pressed hard enough to do anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:08:32-08:00","id":316552,"title":"","content":"The upshot in American politics is money. And that stinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T01:02:27-08:00","id":317095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=315427#post315427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better still, go with the even more simple solution of every legal resident getting a fixed living expense from the government that covers all basic needs (and tie the amount into a basket of CoL expenses), and with one higher-tax stroke you eliminate the need for welfare, minimum wage and all the welfare-to-work headaches that go along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, I see where you're coming from, but...no. Just, no. The economics of that is totally infeasible.<br /> <br /> If you kept it to unemployed people (like food stamps or whatever), then that'd <i>work</i> (although be far from ideal), but still, not great, economically speaking. (Not saying welfare should go away entirely, but it does tend to contribute to inflation and that, which can be problematic at times. Tolerable problem, to be sure, and better than the alternative, but still a problem.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T01:41:17-08:00","id":317112,"title":"","content":"Let's be frank, enforcing equality in such way is infeasible, but again, my controversial opinion is that people are not equal because each one of us is born into different circumstances and with different capabilities. So, lynch me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T01:48:37-08:00","id":317120,"title":"","content":"@Kat And I thought I was the only one... Voicing such an opinion out loud can surely earn you a beating though :P or at the very least looks that want to kill you. Believe me, I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T02:08:45-08:00","id":317134,"title":"","content":"Why, exactly is in economically infeasible (why it is politically so is pretty obvious)?<br /> <br /> An underfunded lower and middle class is a massive drain on economic growth, thus increases inflation. A highly disparity in wealth such as exists in the USA increases money supply (aka more wealth concentrated in the highest brackets is generally linked to that money being put in the money supply instead of being spent); which also increases inflation.<br /> <br /> So what is economically infeasible about redistributing - through taxes - in the fashion Odd_Canuck describes? It should actually decrease inflation, not increase it, since it would draw the rate of economic growth and the rate of the growth of a money supply closer together, and therefore suppress inflation.<br /> <br /> Inflation is a bit of a boogeyman in all this anyway. Most economists agree that a low level of inflation is actually a good thing, and most developed countries have a multitude of ways to adjust inflation rates through policy to maintain the level of inflation they feel is optimal.<br /> <br /> The whole economic argument for a social safety net is that it is actually better for the economy to keep people from falling into economic hardship through government assistance than it is to let people go solely with the whims of their personal situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T02:13:14-08:00","id":317137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317112#post317112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's be frank, enforcing equality in such way is infeasible, but again, my controversial opinion is that people are not equal because each one of us is born into different circumstances and with different capabilities. So, lynch me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a lefty doesn't mean trying to enforce some satirical notion of equality. It isn't about some Randian strawman about how redistributive policies are attacks on those born with social and genetic advantages.<br /> <br /> The point is that economies are actually better off if you limit (not eliminate) inequality. One way to accomplish this is by providing a baseline set of resources. It doesn't stop rich people from having more assets than everyone else. It just means that the difference is less extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T02:47:55-08:00","id":317206,"title":"","content":"If basic goods are provided for free by the government, then the cost of living goes entirely sideways. Also, competition gets entirely shafted (for example, how many businesses make their living on selling milk? Or bread?), so by providing them means, most likely, that the government buys the milk from milk producers, then provides it for free to everyone. But then who pays for the transport of the milk? The wages of the drivers? The maintenance of the trucks? Say we cover that with taxes. But then what about truck repairers who don't repair the government milk trucks, but repair, say, corn trucks? Are they also paid through tax? Let's say yes, that all service necessary to provide these basic goods is paid for by tax.<br /> <br /> What about people who fix jewellery trucks (yes, I'm getting a bit silly here, I'm going for illustrative)? Jewellery is pretty solidly not a necessary good, so the jewellery movers have to pay for that out of pocket. What about truck parts, which are necessary for milk trucks but also for jewellery trucks, even though those parts are often applicable to both trucks (because they're the same model because it's really efficient and let's face it there's only so many ways to put a truck together). Do they need to enquire to the use of the trucks before they provide the part so they know how to handle payment? Then what's stopping lying? What if the truck is used for milk one day of the week, and jewellery four days? What about the different value of bread vs milk vs apples? What about research to improve the shelf life of milk?<br /> <br /> You begin to grasp my point. The situation rapidly becomes insanely complicated and riddled with corruption. The idea of minimum wage is that it covers the cost of living for that person, thus working within the system than requiring a wholesale overhaul which'd be way less efficient and probably collapse anyway (an extreme form of this is communism/socialism, and while what you propose wouldn't be the same thing, it'd be close enough that a lot of the same problems would develop). Now, obviously the idea of minimum wage is not applied perfectly, and that certainly needs addressing (seriously, what is it with America and being unable to grasp simple concepts? No offence intended to any Americans reading this, your county just looks nuts from the outside).<br /> <br /> And a little inflation isn't a problem, even desirable as you point out. But the problem is when it's not a little, bringing it down is a bitch, and building 2-3% inflation (likely more, but let's pretend) right into the system just jacks the 'resting point' higher. You could readjust wages to compensate, but you'd be better off just adjusting minimum wage. Simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T03:54:31-08:00","id":317251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is that economies are actually better off if you limit (not eliminate) inequality. One way to accomplish this is by providing a baseline set of resources. It doesn't stop rich people from having more assets than everyone else. It just means that the difference is less extreme. </div> </div> </div>What is baseline set of resources then? I mean, I can understand providing most basic food and housing needs, but above that it's debatable what is baseline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T06:55:32-08:00","id":317345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317206#post317206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If basic goods are provided for free by the government, then the cost of living goes entirely sideways.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is talking about the Government giving milk away for free. We are talking about the fact that society has acknowledged that it isn't fair to expect people to survive on $0/year, but there are so many different programs we can simplify things by resetting the minimum income from $0 to something baseline livable and let people buy their own damned milk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T09:23:28-08:00","id":317440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317206#post317206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If basic goods are provided for free by the government, then the cost of living goes entirely sideways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing I didn't suggest anything of the sort then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317206#post317206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of minimum wage is that it covers the cost of living for that person,</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is amazingly close to what I actually proposed (giving people a regular payment to cover the cost of living), with the distinction that it's handled automatically, so that it doesn't become either pointless (the current US minimum wage is at it's lowest buying power since it was instituted) or a point of political manipulation (see the various states that have mandated drug tests for the sake of looking tough on drug use at a wasteful expense, and that are expanding it to include employment insurance).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317206#post317206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a little inflation isn't a problem, even desirable as you point out. But the problem is when it's not a little, bringing it down is a bitch, and building 2-3% inflation (likely more, but let's pretend) right into the system just jacks the 'resting point' higher. You could readjust wages to compensate, but you'd be better off just adjusting minimum wage. Simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like how we've done such a wonderful job of it to date? Hence why it should be automated, because once the system is in place the LESS people can tweak it for their own ends, the better for the people.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only real arguments that can be made(that I'm aware of) against my proposal are first that simply handing people the money doesn't prevent the abuse of that money by spending it on drugs or other addictions, and given roughly 10% of the US population has or has had issues in the past with addictions, that is a concern. It is however one that I think should be handled from the angle of getting someone into treatment and maybe as part of that help, get the money somewhat automated for the person... money comes in, portion automatically goes to the landlord for rent, portion gets sent to the grocery store that will do some deliveries, and the other critical to life stuff.<br /> <br /> The next counter argument is that simply *giving* people the cost of living is going to result in people simply living off of that amount and not bothering to actually go work, and thus being a continual drain on society. To which my answer is largely... So what? There are two forces at play there, first is that we are rapidly approaching the point in western society where automation or simply advanced tools takes care of the rote labour and low end jobs. At the same time, there is a large portion of the population that are skilled enough to go into more advanced jobs. This is why there are 20-50 applicants for every job opening at McDonalds, because jobs are disappearing faster and faster from the middle range. With technology changes, this is going to start happening more and more at the lower-paying jobs as well. This is why we have burger making robots, and part-finding robots at hardware chains, they're far cheaper than people. Society has to adapt to the fact that people will not be able to find any sort of manual labor or other near-minimum wage job. Now, there have been psychological studies done on the societal parasite effect that is feared. Since nobody has actually done it, the projections are rough, anywhere from 3-11% depending on how things shake out could end up in that state. Most of the rest are projected to move into creative content production. Writing, videos and such.<br /> <br /> The biggest one is of course the cost, and there's straight up no real way around that. You can get some of the money because you'd be doing away with other social welfare programmes at both the state and federal levels, <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T10:53:37-08:00","id":317571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317206#post317206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You begin to grasp my point. The situation rapidly becomes insanely complicated and riddled with corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point is a massive strawman that doesn't actually address anything said. And the current situation is already complicated and riddle with corruption. The goal of ideas such as Odd_Canuck's is to simply the system (the USA currently has over 125 assistance programs just on the federal level, including ones that let millionaires collect federal assistance benefits) to eliminate those complications, and make the corruption easier to identify and stop. It is similar to arguments for the USA to have massive tax reform because the current tax code is a gigantic mess of complication, and that complication generally screws over poor people while letting the rich and corporations avoid taxes they should be paying; aka is riddled with corruption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a little inflation isn't a problem, even desirable as you point out. But the problem is when it's not a little, bringing it down is a bitch, and building 2-3% inflation (likely more, but let's pretend) right into the system just jacks the 'resting point' higher. You could readjust wages to compensate, but you'd be better off just adjusting minimum wage. Simpler. </div> </div> </div>You haven't actually explained why such redistributive programs would increase inflation if implemented properly. For complaining about Americans not grasping simple concepts, inflation is a fairly complex concept, but you're not seeming to address any of the fundamentals about it. You're just making a claim and calling it a fact even when challenged to demonstrate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317251#post317251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is baseline set of resources then? I mean, I can understand providing most basic food and housing needs, but above that it's debatable what is baseline.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why we have things like cost of living indexes and similar metrics. We know how to study economics well enough to be able to figure out where to set a poverty line, which means we can figure out how much people need to make sure they don't fall below it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317440#post317440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is amazingly close to what I actually proposed (giving people a regular payment to cover the cost of living), with the distinction that it's handled automatically, so that it doesn't become either pointless (the current US minimum wage is at it's lowest buying power since it was instituted) or a point of political manipulation (see the various states that have mandated drug tests for the sake of looking tough on drug use at a wasteful expense, and that are expanding it to include employment insurance).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, your proposal also has foundations in the writings of the founding fathers. There were a few that essentially proposed the same thing (well, they proposed paying white men anyway), on the ethical basis of the fact that no US citizen actually has more of a claim to ownership of the land than any other, and the government should pay everyone to compensate for the government removing that claim to the land to recognize ownership (and continue the ownership based on British law before hand) as we still do now.<br /> <br /> Hell, Alaska has this as an actual policy (and Alaska is not exactly a liberal leaning state). Residents of Alaska get paid by their state government to compensate them for the natural resources the government sells to companies. It's not a CoL linked thing, but it is proof that writing a check to all of your citizens doesn't destroy the economy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only real arguments that can be made(that I'm aware of) against my proposal are first that simply handing people the money doesn't prevent the abuse of that money by spending it on drugs or other addictions, and given roughly 10% of the US population has or has had issues in the past with addictions, that is a concern. </div> </div> </div>And there's plenty of evidence that this concern isn't based in a rational assessment of human behavior. Most studies of the linking of poverty and addiction demonstrate two key points. First, there's a level of addiction that's always present that defies socio-economic status (aka rich people do drugs too). Second, poverty causes drug abuse. Most people, when successful raised out of poverty, reduce or eliminate their consumption of drugs, rather than go spend their money on more drugs and live in shit conditions.<br /> <br /> There's actually some good studies that debunk some of the thinking on how dangerous drugs are. There's the old studies about how rodents will starve themselves to death getting high. But it's also long since demonstrated that this effect only occurs in significant portions of rodents if they're in complete isolation. The more positive social interactions they have, and the more enrichment they have available to them, their drug use drops drastically and they don't kill themselves for whichever drug they're testing.<br /> <br /> Tying government assistance to drug screening makes drug abuse worse, not better. And it does nothing to prevent other common behavioral conditions (such as gambling) that people use as escape mechanisms from stress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since nobody has actually done it, the projections are rough, anywhere from 3-11% depending on how things shake out could end up in that state. </div> </div> </div>Oddly, mainstream economics considers an unemployment rate in this range (where in this range is a huge debate) a <i>good</i> thing. Actual 100% employment is not a good sign. So the idea that there would be some &quot;parasites&quot; on such a system is actually not a huge economic issue as long as those that seek employment can get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The biggest one is of course the cost, and there's straight up no real way around that. You can get some of the money because you'd be doing away with other social welfare programmes at both the state and federal levels, </div> </div> </div>In the USA, though getting this passed is obviously not going to happen, the cost is not hard to get to.<br /> <br /> If you were to eliminate all current state and federal assistance programs, divide up the amount of money they give out equally amongst all citizens, and cut everyone from infant to senior the same check... you'd get ~$3,000/year for everyone (though funneling that state money into a federal program doesn't work, but it is to illustrate a point, not be an actual policy). So two parents with two children would be getting ~$12,000 on top of what they make working. Just consolidating everything like that, and paying zero attention to who actually needs that money and who doesn't, the amount we're already spending turns out to be rather significant sum as it is. And there would be savings regarding reducing the amount of bureaucracy to handle all of this (hey, small government socialist solutions!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T12:13:14-08:00","id":317618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why we have things like cost of living indexes and similar metrics. We know how to study economics well enough to be able to figure out where to set a poverty line, which means we can figure out how much people need to make sure they don't fall below it. </div> </div> </div>If that means only providing most basic needs, I'm fine. Because I'm tad wary about giving out enough money to afford things humans don't really need for survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T12:23:58-08:00","id":317628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317618#post317618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that means only providing most basic needs, I'm fine. Because I'm tad wary about giving out enough money to afford things humans don't really need for survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>But people need <i>happiness</i> for survival. People need <i>opportunity</i> to get ahead of where they are in the game. You have to ensure the safety net provides more than &quot;the most basic needs&quot;, or it's not a safety net at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T12:30:43-08:00","id":317644,"title":"","content":"Happiness is a subjective notion.<br /> <br /> As of opportunity, I believe actual programs geared towards training people for jobs most suitable for them has advantage over giving money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T12:49:46-08:00","id":317657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317644#post317644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happiness is a subjective notion.<br /> <br /> As of opportunity, I believe actual programs geared towards training people for jobs most suitable for them has advantage over giving money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, happiness is incredibly subjective, which is why you have to allow room for people to at least give it a shot. If people have enough that they're not destitute, they have the opportunity to seek training or education for jobs that are actually suitable for them. Or spend time developing new ways of being happy that they can then sell to fanboys like you and me. Or build small neighborhood restaurants so that people can eat well and cheaply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T13:05:37-08:00","id":317662,"title":"","content":"Once upon a time in the US, minimum wage was enough for a single person. And if you were working a temporary summer job, you could make enough to pay tuition for university for a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T13:07:47-08:00","id":317664,"title":"","content":"That's quite idealistic statement, but I have no illusions about it working smoothly in real life. Myself I would likely reject such help with no attachments as I find satisfaction from improving my own lot with sheer effort, and treasure every earnings I can get at the age of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T13:59:09-08:00","id":317691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317664#post317664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's quite idealistic statement, but I have no illusions about it working smoothly in real life. Myself I would likely reject such help with no attachments as I find satisfaction from improving my own lot with sheer effort, and treasure every earnings I can get at the age of mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you reject all of your available tax deductions, too? We're talking about a tax structure designed to support the economic system we claim we want: Where everyone has the tools to rise up out of poverty into the middle class but it takes tremendous and constant effort to be stay rich. Where there are always middle class consumers to purchase products and qualified workers to manufacture and sell them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T14:28:20-08:00","id":317702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317664#post317664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myself I would likely reject such help with no attachments as I find satisfaction from improving my own lot with sheer effort, and treasure every earnings I can get at the age of mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you my find this emotionally fulfilling, it is ultimately an illusion. There's no such thing as improving your own lot with sheer effort alone. You don't have the resources which improve your lot without the efforts of others. You don't have the systems to operate within to improve your lot without others. There are always attachments, even if they are not built into the specific structure of a given program, because that program doesn't exist within a vacuum. Getting a check from your government just for being a citizen is not a situation without attachments, because being a citizen is a condition with attachments; even if the check you're getting doesn't alter your responsibilities as a citizen.<br /> <br /> We're social organisms. We need each others to survive and prosper. We even need a certain amount of inequality. But you can't have wealth without other people (wealth is inherently based on a social contract of worth), so you can't have more wealth than you started with without other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T16:00:52-08:00","id":317747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=317644#post317644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happiness is a subjective notion.<br /> <br /> As of opportunity, I believe actual programs geared towards training people for jobs most suitable for them has advantage over giving money.</div> </div> </div> </div>honestly that's why I tend to feel that most education should be readily available to people no matter what income they have.<br /> <br /> I'm not a complete idiot, I know we're never going to get rid the legacy admissions to high end universities or the practice of the Gentleman's C, I just want society to reach a point where if someone has an interest in post secondary education they're not gambling their future on it as currently happens. Should not matter if it's a woman from a upper middle class town or a guy from the bad part of Oakland, if they have the drive to get educated, they shouldn't be getting saddled with a massive debt in doing so.<br /> <br /> Again, this is something that is starting to have the parts fall into place, as more and more colleges and universities offer more and more of the course content available freely online, it gets closer to the situation where we could do this as a society... again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T17:01:35-08:00","id":317800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> honestly that's why I tend to feel that most education should be readily available to people no matter what income they have. </div> </div> </div>If someone lives in Europe than probably free <i>higher</i> education is a norm rather than exception, even in countries not ruled by socialists (like Poland, socialists here have no chance to become a major political power in near future)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T02:02:37-08:00","id":318095,"title":"","content":"Not free, but very, very cheap compared to the nightmare that seems to be in the USA. I can say I know of no one that got indebted for life for going to the university, but I know of some that couldn't afford it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T02:38:18-08:00","id":318116,"title":"","content":"Those who could not afford it must have been really destitute since I do not come from affluent background yet made it and finished my major.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T03:52:14-08:00","id":318150,"title":"","content":"Here in Portugal University costs 1k per YEAR at most and you can apply for support from the state if you can't afford it.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Private University which are around 3k per year but most you don't have to pay if your grades are above a certain value and on the other hand they are not as good as the public ones anyway.<br /> <br /> the 12 grades before university are actually FREE. Since 1st Grade and until you graduate High School, education is completely free. The only thing you spend money on are notebooks, pens and one book for each subject you have. Again, you can ask support from the state if you can't afford it or talk to various organizations that supply used books.<br /> <br /> Education and Health in the USA are a nightmare. I try not to bash any countries since mine is far from perfect, but seeing that people actually OPPOSE free education and free health care shocks me! (health care is very sensitive subject for me since I had a very bad and cruel experience in a Miami Hospital)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T06:12:07-08:00","id":318191,"title":"","content":"No one goes to university without going into massive debt in the US, unless one is already wealthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T09:01:37-08:00","id":318296,"title":"","content":"^^Even solidly right wing parties here do not oppose free healthcare and education unless they are minor parties for which actually getting into parliament would be a success. Murrican politics in that field is aberration rather the norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T11:36:50-08:00","id":318381,"title":"","content":"Checking in as a big old socialist here. To sum my politics up in a sentence: I find the idea that, in a civilization where we have the resources to make every single human being safe and comfortable, we still hold on to the idea that someone should have to <i>earn </i>a safe and comfortable existence by producing capital for those richer than themselves to be morally repugnant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T12:48:44-08:00","id":318422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find the idea that, in a civilization where we have the resources to make every single human being safe and comfortable, </div> </div> </div>To be honest, with growing population and depleting resources your ideal becomes more distant from realization with each decade. It would better for mankind if the population stabilized and stopped growing rapidly. Thankfully that is happening in Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T13:52:41-08:00","id":318465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those who could not afford it must have been really destitute since I do not come from affluent background yet made it and finished my major. </div> </div> </div>Is not so much the university fees themselves but the asociated cost of having to pay a rent to go living where the university is, plus all the regular costs of food, power, etc and transportation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T13:55:04-08:00","id":318468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=318422#post318422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, with growing population and depleting resources your ideal becomes more distant from realization with each decade. It would better for mankind if the population stabilized and stopped growing rapidly. Thankfully that is happening in Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually the interesting thing. While there's no obvious direct single point of causation we can point at, pretty much all western countries seem to have stabilizing and declining birth rates, largely in proportion to availability of birth control and general health and wellness. So helping people to be educated, not starving seems to be an effective meta-method to stabilize or even decrease the population.<br /> <br /> As for depleting resources, it's a highly subjective thing. The whole Peak Oil thing has been a standard &quot;it's going to start happening in the next 5 years!&quot; battle cry since the '70's, and continues to be based the rather unrealistic assumption that even as extraction costs rise, the cost of oil and fuel will remain relatively low. There also tends to be a lot bias towards using the same things in the same ways and ignoring a continually changing marketplace.<br /> <br /> Right now, we have insanely cheap oil, over the coming decades it's expected that natural gas will take over much of the demand. Can we continue for the next century relying on just oil or even oil and gas? No. However that's why we have science and engineering. We easily have the capacity to provide power for the next few thousand years at current and projected levels of consumption, with the technology we have now. And that's with the technology we have now, there are reasons we invest in fusion research and development, as well as the bio generated hydrocarbon researches, because with those we are sorted out for our needs for even longer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T14:00:27-08:00","id":318471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=318422#post318422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, with growing population and depleting resources your ideal becomes more distant from realization with each decade. It would better for mankind if the population stabilized and stopped growing rapidly. Thankfully that is happening in Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will try to summarise how I would reply to many of the posts I missed and have not read.<ul><li>We are not faced with resource scarcity. This is a concept first conceived by Malthus and has never proven true in real life. I have witnessed some of the absurdities of capitalism in Greece, where supermarkets opt to throw out large portions of their inventory, rather than give it away for free (with 60+% of under-30s unemployment, it would make sense). Technological advances will, for the most part, take care of those concerns.</li> <li>The problem with the USSR remains with contemporary liberal democracies, specifically groups of people that more or less avoid scrutiny and hold unchecked power. It is far from democratic, to be deemed a citizen only once in four years. An inclusive, direct democratic model, is much needed. This leaves, however, the question of inequalities in the economy.</li> <li>Soviet economy, despite its accomplishments (zero unemployment, zero poverty, zero homelessness, near-zero crime rates) had one fatal flaw. It was based around a pyramid model, that was ineffective and entrusted a group of increasingly aged bureaucrats with the power that was eventually turned against the very socialist state it was supposed to uphold. The collapse of the USSR was, in fact, due to the elite realising they had more to earn from capitalism (becoming the oligarchs).</li> </ul>Not enough time to elaborate more, but will do soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T14:10:02-08:00","id":318496,"title":"","content":"I don't think the issue of over-population is at odds with the ideal Gabby professed.<br /> <br /> For example, one of the tools we have to ensure that everyone has what they need to have a safe and comfortable existence is population control.<br /> <br /> And it is worth noting that higher standards of living are associated with smaller families (aka less population growth). You don't even need any real policy systems on the subject in most cases. It's a natural psychological process.<br /> <br /> But in the end, the point was if we can provide safe and comfortable living with the resources we have, we should. Overpopulation reaching the tipping point where that if statement is not satisfied doesn't damage the moral ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T14:36:00-08:00","id":318504,"title":"","content":"Population control is scary but likely necessary. Next year it was projected that half of the world's nations will live in &quot;water-stressed&quot; societies. I'm reminded of something; <a href=\"http://www.news.com.au/world/hillary-clinton-tries-to-silence-brave-bindi/story-fndir2ev-1226560803039\" target=\"_blank\">Hillary Clinton tries to silence Bindi Irwin on population growth</a>...<i>The young conservationist, daughter of the late &quot;Crocodile Hunter&quot; Steve Irwin, was asked to write 800-1000 words on why she had chosen to devote her life's work to wildlife conservation. But after writing exactly 1000 words urging society to address overpopulation, the former first lady's department returned it for final approval with most of it edited out. &quot;It's interesting that she was asked to write an essay about the environment and included the consideration of population (growth) and they returned her essay edited and completely edited that out,&quot; she said. &quot;So Bindi wrote to Hillary Clinton's organisation and said 'what happened to freedom of speech? This is my opinion and I don't want that edited out'.&quot; The tough-talking teen \u2013 who onscreen has freed Willy, fought pirate animal poachers and hosted Bindi's Boot Camp \u2013 pulled the essay from the publication in anticipation of a response.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T15:36:44-08:00","id":318539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We are not faced with resource scarcity. This is a concept first conceived by Malthus and has never proven true in real life. I have witnessed some of the absurdities of capitalism in Greece, where supermarkets opt to throw out large portions of their inventory, rather than give it away for free (with 60+% of under-30s unemployment, it would make sense). Technological advances will, for the most part, take care of those concerns. </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly concerned we might one day face the problem of providing rare elements for our technology as Third World starts to catch up with Euroamerican societies and demand for them increases.<br /> <br /> And there is the problem of scarcity of fresh water that we might face. I don't think any climate change short of cataclysms on scale of Yellowstone supervulcano blowing up will endanger survival of human species, but it will make life more difficult in general. We are better off trying to stay at the population level we already have, and then if colonization of other celestial bodies becomes a thing, send away large portion of population so remaining people have it easier.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T17:45:10-08:00","id":318580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=318539#post318539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm honestly concerned we might one day face the problem of providing rare elements for our technology as Third World starts to catch up with Euroamerican societies and demand for them increases.<br /> <br /> And there is the problem of scarcity of fresh water that we might face. I don't think any climate change short of cataclysms on scale of Yellowstone supervulcano blowing up will endanger survival of human species, but it will make life more difficult in general. We are better off trying to stay at the population level we already have, and then if colonization of other celestial bodies becomes a thing, send away large portion of population so remaining people have it easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm far less worries, given most of the rare elements we need today are secondary mining products... as in they're used so little, we don't actually mine FOR them, we just extract them as side effect of other mining projects. As for general minerals and metals... well, adjusting for inflation, the costs to produce have done nothing but go down. I'd wait for it to level out or even increase before worrying about that myself.<br /> <br /> Water... water is another thing. The big problem with water right now is much the same as with food... it's not that there isn't enough in the world, it's that it isn't where the people need to consume it. That is mostly something that can only be addressed by either mass migration of populations, or using technology to produce clean water. Unfortunately the cheapest/easiest way to do that is with desalination plants and the technology there is in flux. It's a low-profit field because nobody wants to pay for water right now, and there are a lot of highly disruptive technologies being developed... building a 20 million dollar plant today might mean it's got the same costs as something that could have 10 times the capacity for the same cost in 5 years.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:11:01-08:00","id":319145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=318422#post318422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, with growing population and depleting resources your ideal becomes more distant from realization with each decade. It would better for mankind if the population stabilized and stopped growing rapidly. Thankfully that is happening in Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>the way wealth and resources are currently concentrated is more of a problem than the sheer number of humans could ever realistically be. We have the resources. We might not always have the resources in the future, but that's a problem our billions of well-educated, comfortable, non-starving thinkers could work on. The only difference between a world where resources are apportioned fairly and our current world is that in the theoretical future when we finally hit a resource crisis, most of us will have spent the previous decades/centuries living like we were already in one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 11-22-2014, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T13:17:49-08:00","id":319262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but that's a problem our billions of well-educated, comfortable, non-starving thinkers </div> </div> </div>I hope that's hyperbole, because not everyone's apt for doing science. Note that even in First World countries not everyone chooses higher education or goes for engineering and scientific majors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T14:24:00-08:00","id":319310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=319262#post319262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that's hyperbole, because not everyone's apt for doing science. Note that even in First World countries not everyone chooses higher education or goes for engineering and scientific majors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty certain that lack of education is how First World countries drop from being &quot;First World.&quot; The Golden age of Islam reveals that quite plainly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T14:40:59-08:00","id":319313,"title":"","content":"Can't speak for Gabby, but I doubt that was intended to be, &quot;everyone will be a thinker/scientist that will solve resource issues in the future.&quot;<br /> <br /> But keep in mind the numbers on disparity here. Lets say 1:30 people has the high level of aptitude you're talking about (completely arbitrary value picked for easy math). That would mean we have over 100 million potential high aptitude people currently held back by living in extreme poverty (as defined by living on less that $2.50 a day).<br /> <br /> Even if &quot;billions&quot; is hyperbole, that's a huge amount of wasted talent.<br /> <br /> You can play with the numbers in any number of ways, but the point remains that we're letting lots of potential talent slip through the cracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T17:04:01-08:00","id":319502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty certain that lack of education is how First World countries drop from being &quot;First World.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Don't see that in the case of Western World.<br /> <br /> ^This math could be complicated also by the fact that not all of people that choose scientific major are people who are innovative enough to contribute to breakthroughs. I mean, there are people who won't create something original, but are good with working on what has been already invented.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it should be so that people could learn to perform what gives them satisfaction anyway. I think that while higher education is something that should be supported, vocational schools unfortunately get often neglected.<br /> <br /> PS. In my case, while my mother pushed me to focus solely on law or become a priest, I chose what I liked more over money and studied linguistics. Well, later on I started studying some law, but only because my goal is to become a sworn translator. I can do what I like and earn lot of money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-22-2014, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T10:45:09-08:00","id":320028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=319502#post319502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't see that in the case of Western World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Examine the US on a state-by-state basis.<br /> Most of the major tech corridors are all in more educated states.<br /> Most of the &quot;red&quot; states are pretty damn poor. Plenty of the ill-educated in several of them have in the past talked of seceding from the union not recognizing that their particular state takes more than it gives in taxes. Meaning that if they were ever successful, they would go from being a part of one of the wealthiest nations in the world to a Third World country the moment secession was finalized.<br /> I do agree that vocational schools are overlooked. It's a problem today that is being shortchanged.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T11:32:13-08:00","id":320083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the &quot;red&quot; states are pretty damn poor. Plenty of the ill-educated in several of them have in the past talked of seceding from the union not recognizing that their particular state takes more than it gives in taxes. Meaning that if they were ever successful, they would go from being a part of one of the wealthiest nations in the world to a Third World country the moment secession was finalized. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, even less well off states are wealthier than a backwater African state. Even poorer post-communist states in Europe fare better than them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T12:44:02-08:00","id":320116,"title":"","content":"The wealth of those states is completely dependent on their continued being part of the union. Not only are most of them reliant on federal money to keep in the black. Most of them have industries that are based on exporting resources to other states (which gets less profitable once you're exporting to another country).<br /> <br /> Those states are wealthier <i>now</i> because the poorer states are being propped up by the richer ones. That's the whole point. Without that support they would quickly down slide economically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T14:13:01-08:00","id":320184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The wealth of those states is completely dependent on their continued being part of the union. Not only are most of them reliant on federal money to keep in the black. Most of them have industries that are based on exporting resources to other states (which gets less profitable once you're exporting to another country).<br /> <br /> Those states are wealthier now because the poorer states are being propped up by the richer ones. That's the whole point. Without that support they would quickly down slide economically. </div> </div> </div>Certainly they would drop in wealth even if not to the level of Third World, but again, I don't think there is any possibility of a secession in modern United States.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T15:09:05-08:00","id":320211,"title":"","content":"That's just shifting the goalposts. You're going from, &quot;they wouldn't be that bad,&quot; to, &quot;it doesn't matter because that would never happen.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T05:22:37-08:00","id":320636,"title":"","content":"Well, certainly they would not be that bad. I cannot imagine them to drop to level of a backwater country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T21:21:31-08:00","id":322396,"title":"","content":"I ended up:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.politicalcompass.org/facebook/pcgraphpng.php?ec=1.50&amp;soc=0.00\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T18:56:22-08:00","id":324040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=318150#post318150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Education and Health in the USA are a nightmare. I try not to bash any countries since mine is far from perfect, but seeing that people actually OPPOSE free education and free health care shocks me! (health care is very sensitive subject for me since I had a very bad and cruel experience in a Miami Hospital)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that it wasn't so much that they opposed basic free healthcare and that, but they had seriously questions about the model being suggested (which put the cost on employers, which <i>is</i> a seriously debatable issue).<br /> <br /> I like Australia's system, where you are entitled to free healthcare... to a point. Basic GPS and even a lot of specialists can be claimed under Medicare, but if you go private the system isn't so overloaded and the physicians <i>tend</i> to be more skilled and such.<br /> <br /> A lot of people just don't have private health and get by just fine. Maybe differences mean the system can't be applied in the US, but it works fine here. Even the overloading of the public health system has started to improve over the last few years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T22:44:20-08:00","id":324229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=324040#post324040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that it wasn't so much that they opposed basic free healthcare and that, but they had seriously questions about the model being suggested (which put the cost on employers, which <i>is</i> a seriously debatable issue).</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately having lived through the debates and discussion on it here (I've lived in California for the last decade), it's actually all that and more.<br /> <br /> There were a number of people that object to it because &quot;Mah Freedom!&quot;... or in other words they maintain the argument that it should not ever be something that is required. A subset of this is the economic argument, if someone is young and healthy there should be no reason for them to pay into a health care system when they are consuming none of it's services/goods.<br /> <br /> There's also a number that object to it because it's (gasp) socialized. It might be a running joke, but there is a not unsizeable minority of people in the US for whom socialism = communism = satan and horrible things.<br /> <br /> And to be frank there's a number of people hate it because it was proposed by a black president. When someone who utterly hates Obama such as the owner of forbes magazine does a piece on why he's good for america and good for rich people, helped the poor and the middle class, and how he has actually surpassed Reagan for a golden age of profitability and improvement and you STILL object to his policies on the basis of overall money and cost, you're not fooling anyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the system specifically, I frankly would have preferred what Obama proposed originally, which was a single payer system, instead we have a mish-mash that still allows for a lot of profit to be gleaned off every level.<br /> <br /> Instead... well, let's go this way, my own experience. After the AHA was passed, every health insurance company jacked up it's rates, under the statement that &quot;well, we really don't want to but Obamacare jacks up the rates. sorry.&quot; After the act swung into effect, I was presented with the same story from the insurance companies. About a decade ago, between the company's contributions and my own, it was costing about $350/month for a single person decently high quality insurance. Getting a similar policy today with both the company and the personal costs, would likely run around $1200/month.<br /> <br /> The costs went up for consumers and businesses alike. Because no actual insurance or medical practices needed to change or really did anything to change in the US. Because there are a lot of inflated and badly standardized numbers and limits all over the place, and unfortunately nothing is actually being done to fix that. To give you an idea of the scope, the same procedure in one hospital might be billed at $3000, at another hospital 15 miles away it could be billed at $30000.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually I'll tell you what, I'll give you a recent example of a current health incident, since I happen to have all the numbers from the offices involved. Non-emergency. A few months back I had a rather large and painful abscess. Went to a walk-in clinic. These are basically places that deal with the non-emergency things that a doctor's office might not be equipped for normally or that need a faster response than a week or so. So go in, get injected with a local, small cut and I am fine and dandy, 15 minutes. The cost for this according to the statement I got would have been $1617 and some change.<br /> <br /> The whole way the system works right now is on a method of overcharging and letting insurance pay the overcharge, it's probably supposed to make people feel good about having dodged that huge expense and more than likely (I've not dug into it, this is just a guess based on human nature) is part of a system to help shift around money from taxable to non-taxable organizations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=324040#post324040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Australia's system, where you are entitled to free healthcare... to a point. Basic GPS and even a lot of specialists can be claimed under Medicare, but if you go private the system isn't so overloaded and the physicians <i>tend</i> to be more skilled and such.<br /> <br /> A lot of people just don't have private health and get by just fine. Maybe differences mean the system can't be applied in the US, but it works fine here. Even the overloading of the public health system has started to improve over the last few years.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not dissimilar to what Canada does in places, and it works fairly well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T17:53:45-08:00","id":383850,"title":"","content":"T