\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/309967-the-thread-of-the-left?p=384097#post384097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm worried that SYRIZA promising things that Greece cannot afford will simply make the situation tumble down.<br /> <br /> I won't be suprised if in the end SYRIZA will be judged by Greeks themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>They plan to deal with national debt how Germany was allowed to deal with its debt in 1953. Austerity and trickle-down has not worked (I speak now as a student of Politics working on a dissertation about political economy) and will only hinder Greece's ability to pay back anything (beyond interest rates).<br /> <br /> Today they announced they are pushing forward with reforms, so that's good for the Greeks (myself included).<br /> There strategy is risky, to be sure, but I will choose to remain hopeful (for now). I am also concerned about<br /> the infamous &quot;democratic deficit&quot; of the EU and its fetishization of austerity, which SYRIZA seems to want to address<br /> Europe-wide.<br /> <br /> So let's see. The new Finance Minister also worked for Valve, so that's good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"P